{
 "description": "The agent library's own scope-binding vectors (spec RFC 0030 §2, Binding a chain to one scope identifier; §3, clause 9; conformance table 3's statement rows and its library rows). Signed once with the RFC's synthetic keys (the Ed25519 seed judgment-pack-delegation-host-01 and the P-256 scalar of 32 bytes of 01) by node:crypto, not by the verifier under test. statements: a chain and the first refusal of steps 1 to 7, or ok, with the link it is at. requests: a call under a chain of statements, by name, at a time inside its validity unless at is given; expect is the admission's refusal, or admit; reads is how many admission reads the host's port is asked. bindings: a gateway source declared to the run's gate under a chain of statements, by name, whose receipts the host verifies (verifyReceipt) and the package does not, fixed to the scope identifier fixed (null for none); expect is the refusal at binding, with a guardrail whose detail holds detail and no call of the source sent, or admit.",
